      "congressionalg7391unit:299:par_000299_000036": {
        "text": "The same question that pends before us hangs upon a hair in the entranced gaze of the labor- ing masses of what we too fondly call \"the mother country.\" I ask my colleague, who spoke so kindly of the German, the English- man, the Scotchman, and the Irishman, whether he is willing to send across the ocean an en- couraging word to the despots of the British Government, and to set an example which will justify them in saying, \"We will withhold from the laboring people this right, for the great democratic republic country has had the ques- tion under discussion, and has decided that people poor and ignorant as are our laboring classes ought not to have the right of suffrage?\" If gentlemen on the other side do, they will hear songs that were not sung in the \" Groves of Blarney.\"",
